WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER, AND WHY THAT MATTERS
================================================================================

Three things travel with this repository that are not ours to license. None of
them is in the repository itself; all three are mounted or downloaded, and a
licence on this repository says nothing about any of them.

1. THE CORPUS — classical Persian poetry, from Ganjoor (ganjoor.net).

   Do not assume it is free to redistribute. Ganjoor's own FAQ, asked directly
   whether its data are free of copyright, answers "لزوماً خیر!" — not
   necessarily. It states that no legal review has been made; that most of the
   content was typed from published books whose own status was never
   established; that editing and compilation can attract rights of their own;
   and that free access must not be read as a licence, the responsibility being
   the reader's.

   Ganjoor's *software* is GPL-3.0. The poetry is not covered by it.

   Checked 2026-08-17. This is why the deployment described in docs/DEPLOY.md
   sits behind a password, and why that password is a requirement rather than
   a precaution.

2. THE LEXICON — karbon's Dehkhoda-derived table of headwords and readings.

   Mounted read-only. Its terms are karbon's question, not this repository's.

3. THE EXPERT FEEDBACK SET — graded verdicts on generated words, exported by
   `tools/export_feedback.py`.

   These are judgements made by named experts about the language. They are not
   code, Apache is not a licence for data, and they were not given to this
   project to give away. The export says so in its own manifest. Ask before
   redistributing.

